# shape_constraint.tkr — the §9.2b shape-constraint-solver ACCEPT channel. A constraint is a
# DISJUNCTION OF CONJUNCTIONS (`<T: Alt1 | Alt2 | …>`, each `Alt` = `Term & Term & …`) over four term
# kinds: form words (`class`/`service [lifetime]`/`struct`), interfaces (conformance), concrete types
# (identity), and the `&`-only `notnull` modifier. One native build carries a scenario per term kind
# plus one per alternative of the spec's own example, so a term that stopped resolving names the row
# that broke. The REJECT twin — every term's refusal — is `examples/regressions/shape_constraint_reject`.

Feature: shape_constraint — §9.2b shape-constraint solver (form words, service lifetime, notnull, concrete types, disjunction of conjunctions)

  Scenario: notnull_alone — `<T: notnull>` (the modifier used alone) admits a non-nullable i64 (→ 1)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario notnull_alone: ok"

  Scenario: class_and_notnull — `<T: class & notnull>` conjoins the modifier with a form word (→ 2)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario class_and_notnull: ok"

  Scenario: struct_form — the `struct` form word admits a value struct (→ 3)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario struct_form: ok"

  Scenario: service_singleton_form — `<T: service singleton>` admits a service DECLARED singleton (→ 4)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario service_singleton_form: ok"

  Scenario: service_bare_form — a lifetime-less `service` admits a transient service (→ 5)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario service_bare_form: ok"

  Scenario: concrete_type_term — the concrete term `str` forces identity and admits `str` (→ 6)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario concrete_type_term: ok"

  Scenario: disjunction_class_alt — alternative 1 (`class & Ifce`) of `<T: class & Ifce | struct & OutraIfce | str>` (→ 7)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario disjunction_class_alt: ok"

  Scenario: disjunction_struct_alt — alternative 2 (`struct & OutraIfce`) of the same disjunction (→ 7)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario disjunction_struct_alt: ok"

  Scenario: disjunction_concrete_alt — alternative 3 (`str`) of the same disjunction (→ 7)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario disjunction_concrete_alt: ok"
